WEBVTT

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:00.800
I'm a manager.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.559
I open the chat interface and

00:00:02.559 --> 00:00:04.580
I ask a highly complex question.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.199
I need an answer that requires

00:00:06.199 --> 00:00:07.840
checking physical inventory in the

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.960
Lakehouse, cross -referencing current

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.040
temperature telemetry in the Eventhouse,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.980
and calculating the financial impact

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.440
using the DAX math in the

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.480
semantic model. That's a huge request.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.420
Right. Does the system extract all

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.600
that data from those three sources,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.560
pull it into some massive new

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.880
temporary database and run the query

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.500
there? No, and understanding this is

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.360
profound for anyone evaluating the

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.040
cost and performance of this system.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.360
The ontology supplies the definitions

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.339
and the mappings.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.100
It acts as the routing intelligence.

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:38.019
But when a consuming experience, like

00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:39.900
a chat interface, actually formulates

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.040
the query, it executes that query

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.040
against the appropriate native underlying

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:44.620
engine.
